From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:53:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mss: send SSR "before shutdown" before
 sysmon stop

Subdevices are stopped in the reverse order they were added. The MSS
driver adds the SSR subdevice before sysmon, so on a graceful stop sysmon
first asks the modem to shut down over SSCTL and only then are the SSR
notifier clients (ath10k on SDM845) told that the modem is about to go
away. By then the modem has already torn down the services those clients
would need to quiesce their hardware, e.g. the WLAN firmware QMI service.

Add the SSR subdevice after sysmon, as qcom_q6v5_pas already does, so
QCOM_SSR_BEFORE_SHUTDOWN reaches the clients while the modem still runs,
which matches the downstream order (SUBSYS_BEFORE_SHUTDOWN, then sysmon
shutdown). Crash handling is unchanged: sysmon skips the shutdown request
on a crash, and the notification still carries the crashed flag.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c
index 2f71ed2fef..0ca760eca6 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c
@@ -2201,13 +2201,20 @@ static int q6v5_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	qcom_add_glink_subdev(rproc, &qproc->glink_subdev, "mpss");
 	qcom_add_smd_subdev(rproc, &qproc->smd_subdev);
 	qcom_add_pdm_subdev(rproc, &qproc->pdm_subdev);
-	qcom_add_ssr_subdev(rproc, &qproc->ssr_subdev, "mpss");
 	qproc->sysmon = qcom_add_sysmon_subdev(rproc, "modem", desc->ssctl_id);
 	if (IS_ERR(qproc->sysmon)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(qproc->sysmon);
 		goto remove_subdevs;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Subdevices are stopped in reverse order, so adding the SSR subdevice
+	 * after sysmon sends the "before shutdown" notification to clients such
+	 * as ath10k while the modem is still running, before sysmon asks it to
+	 * shut down.
+	 */
+	qcom_add_ssr_subdev(rproc, &qproc->ssr_subdev, "mpss");
+
 	ret = rproc_add(rproc);
 	if (ret)
 		goto remove_sysmon_subdev;
@@ -2219,9 +2226,9 @@ static int q6v5_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 
 remove_sysmon_subdev:
+	qcom_remove_ssr_subdev(rproc, &qproc->ssr_subdev);
 	qcom_remove_sysmon_subdev(qproc->sysmon);
 remove_subdevs:
-	qcom_remove_ssr_subdev(rproc, &qproc->ssr_subdev);
 	qcom_remove_smd_subdev(rproc, &qproc->smd_subdev);
 	qcom_remove_glink_subdev(rproc, &qproc->glink_subdev);
 detach_proxy_pds:
@@ -2240,8 +2247,8 @@ static void q6v5_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	rproc_del(rproc);
 
 	qcom_q6v5_deinit(&qproc->q6v5);
-	qcom_remove_sysmon_subdev(qproc->sysmon);
 	qcom_remove_ssr_subdev(rproc, &qproc->ssr_subdev);
+	qcom_remove_sysmon_subdev(qproc->sysmon);
 	qcom_remove_pdm_subdev(rproc, &qproc->pdm_subdev);
 	qcom_remove_smd_subdev(rproc, &qproc->smd_subdev);
 	qcom_remove_glink_subdev(rproc, &qproc->glink_subdev);
